## Managed calls through msil-ld (ImplementationPlan.md 5.20, milestone
## MC-1): binding (5.20.7 MK1), the objects' stubs (5.20.6 MW1) and the
## stub-internal rows of 5.20.13. calls.ll is the IR clang writes for one
## managed-call declaration of each form of 5.20.2 MA1-MA3 (5.20.4 MR1, MR2,
## MR4: a declaration '__msil_mc.<symbol>' with the msil-managed-* attributes
## and an operand of !msil.managed.calls), with a main that calls each one:
## a static method over every listing primitive, float32/float64, unmanaged
## pointers, object/string/class/array parameters and a string result, a
## constructor with a UTF-8 string, UTF-16 and UTF-32 strings, bool in and
## out, char, a value type in and out by boxed handle, enums over int32,
## int64 and uint8 (signed char for the uint8 one: only the width is
## checked), enums after a plain parameter and after a 'this' handle,
## GCHandle in and out, a virtual property getter (callvirt), an instance
## method (callvirt), a value-type constructor (newobj, then box), a
## value-type instance method (through unbox; see the access forms below)
## and the methods a value type inherits from System.ValueType and
## System.Object (GetHashCode(), GetType()), a static field (ldsfld),
## instance fields of a class and of a value type (ldfld), arrays of a
## primitive and of a class (newarr), a nested type's constructor and a
## nested type in a signature, msil_catch with a derived type before its
## base and a BCL exception, and an ASSEMBLY argument. The members are
## Inputs/fakepack/FakeWidgets.il's, over the core library FakeRuntime.il.
## llc compiles calls.ll for x86_64-pc-windows-msvc-msil,
## x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu-msil and msil64-unknown-dotnet.
## - MW1 as amended in section 12 (2026-11-04): a stub is an internal
##   method of the object and, as 5.8.5 C3 requires of every MethodDef with
##   a body, a LOCAL FUNCTION symbol of the object's link-info symbols:
##   --link-info prints one defined 'FUNCTION LOCAL' symbol
##   '__msil_mc.<symbol>' per stub (the SYMTAB checks), no GLOBAL
##   or WEAK '__msil_mc' symbol (a stub is never exported, imported or bound
##   late), and 'main' is a defined global symbol.
## - With --reference (MK1), each object links without a diagnostic; every
##   member access is a MemberRef of [FakeWidgets] with the signature the
##   declaration wrote (the end-to-end agreement of the signature parser of
##   llvm/include/llvm/CLI/ManagedSignature.h with msil-ld's binder), each
##   type token of a conversion (castclass, box, unbox, unbox.any, isinst,
##   newarr) names its type there, the stub with msil_catch has one filter
##   clause, and 5.20.13's stub-internal members (GCHandle's Alloc,
##   ToIntPtr, FromIntPtr and get_Target, UTF8Encoding's and
##   UTF32Encoding's constructors, Encoding::GetString(uint8*, int32) and
##   String::.ctor(char*)) bind to [FakeRuntime]. Each stub is a method
##   '__msil_mc.<symbol>'. ASSEMBLY (MA4) names the scope of text output
##   only: no 'ContosoText' reaches the image. The images refer to
##   FakeRuntime and FakeWidgets only, never to mscorlib or [msil.bcl].
## - The access of a 'this-val' or 'this-gch' instance method (5.20.3 MS5,
##   5.20.5 ML2 (2) and 5.20.7 MK2 as amended in section 12, 2026-11-04, by
##   the row that supersedes the 'constrained. V' + 'callvirt' row): llc
##   writes the placeholder 'constrained. V' then 'callvirt V::M', and
##   msil-ld rewrites that site in place after binding (the ACCESS and
##   TACCESS checks, ordered, on the linked images). For a member V declares
##   (Contoso.Point::Sum(); without references the 'this-gch' table row
##   GCHandle::Free()), the 6 bytes of the prefix become 6 'nop's and
##   'callvirt' becomes 'call V::M'. For a member V only inherits
##   (System.ValueType::GetHashCode(), and the non-virtual
##   System.Object::GetType(); the binder's base-chain search finds them in
##   FakeRuntime.il), the prefix stays and the MemberRef's parent becomes
##   the declaring type D: 'constrained. V' then 'callvirt [FakeRuntime]D::M'.
##   No linked image keeps 'constrained. V' + 'callvirt V::M'.
##   managed-calls-lto.test has the final forms that LTO code generation
##   writes directly, managed-calls-checks.test MK2's refusal of an access
##   in none of the three shapes.
## - Without references only the built-in table binds (MK1): table.ll's
##   calls, every member a table row after MC-1's block
##   (Environment::GetCommandLineArgs(), Marshal::StringToHGlobalUni(string)
##   from UTF-8, UTF-16 and UTF-32, GCHandle::Free() through a 'this'
##   GCHandle, BitConverter::GetBytes(int32), the EntryPointNotFoundException
##   constructor with msil_catch of DecoderFallbackException,
##   Exception::get_HResult() through a 'this' handle,
##   Buffer::MemoryCopy(void*, void*, int64, int64) and
##   Marshal::AllocHGlobal(native int)), link without a diagnostic and refer
##   to [mscorlib] only.
## - An interface (Contoso.IWidget, FakeWidgets.il): iface.ll's 'this-obj'
##   call of the interface method Score() links with --reference without a
##   diagnostic, and its stub casts the handle's target to the interface
##   ('castclass [FakeWidgets]Contoso.IWidget') and calls it with
##   'callvirt'; iface-val.ll declares the interface as 'valuetype
##   Contoso.IWidget' ('this-val') and gets T-M16 (an interface is a
##   reference type, 5.20.7 MK3).
## - A wrong return type is the binder's error with its overload list
##   (5.11.9): bad-ret.ll asks for int32 Measure(), FakeWidgets defines
##   int64 Measure().
## - Without references, a member outside the table is 5.11.7's
##   '.NET member '<member>' is not in msil-ld's built-in mscorlib table; pass --reference=<reference assemblies>'
##   (nomember.ll: System.Environment::Exit(int32), a member of a table
##   type), and so is a type outside the table, whether it is the type of
##   the member (notype.ll: Contoso.Widget) or an msil_catch type
##   (nocatch.ll: System.IO.IOException).
## - A -shared library whose exported function makes a managed call exports
##   that function and not the stub: no '__msil_mc' name in its symbol
##   table or among the members of its export class, on
##   x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu-msil and msil64-unknown-dotnet, and on
##   msil64-unknown-dotnet also for bitcode through LTO (net.head).
## - MR2 (reason 4, 5.20.4): mr2a.ll declares f with msil_method and
##   defines g, which calls it; mr2b.ll declares a plain 'int f(int)' and
##   main calls f and g. The stub is '__msil_mc.f', never 'f', so the plain
##   declaration stays undefined: 'undefined symbol: f', referenced by
##   mr2b.o's main, on a host triple and on msil64-unknown-dotnet
##   (managed-calls-lto.test has the bitcode form).
## managed-calls-checks.test has msil-ld's checks of 5.20.7 (T-M7, T-M8,
## T-M9, T-M16, T-M18, T-M23), managed-calls-lto.test the LTO forms (MK5,
## MW3, T-M17) and the same checks in LTO links,
## managed-calls-forwarders.test the exported and start-up managed calls
## (T-M17's second form, T-M21, T-M23's forwarder form),
## managed-calls-units.test T-M17 between the units that still declare a
## managed call, in every link mode, managed-calls-address.test T-M10 and a
## unit's own T-M17 in LTO links, before LTO's optimizer,
## managed-calls-text-checks.test the run-time checks of --lto-emit-asm
## text, managed-calls-late.test the archive members that LTO's code
## generation extracts, managed-calls-assembly.test ASSEMBLY, and
## managed-calls-inherited.test the static methods that a struct or an enum
## only inherits.

# REQUIRES: llvm-cil-dump
# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t && cd %t
# RUN: mkdir refs
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeRuntime.yaml -o refs/FakeRuntime.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeWidgets.yaml -o refs/FakeWidgets.dll
# DEFINE: %{crash} = --implicit-check-not="PLEASE submit" --implicit-check-not="Stack dump" \
# DEFINE:   --implicit-check-not="LLVM ERROR"
# DEFINE: %{err} = FileCheck %s %{crash} --implicit-check-not=error: --implicit-check-not=warning:

## MW1, then the links with references, on each triple.
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj -mtriple=x86_64-pc-windows-msvc-msil calls.ll -o win.o
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump --link-info win.o > win.sym
# RUN: FileCheck %s %{crash} --check-prefix=SYMTAB --input-file=win.sym
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SYMHDR --input-file=win.sym \
# RUN:   --implicit-check-not="{{(GLOBAL|WEAK) .*__msil_mc}}"
# RUN: msil-ld win.o --reference=refs -o win.exe 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump win.exe > win.txt
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=BIND,STUBS --input-file=win.txt
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ACCESS --input-file=win.txt
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=REFS --input-file=win.txt --implicit-check-not=assemblyref \
# RUN:   --implicit-check-not=mscorlib --implicit-check-not=msil.bcl --implicit-check-not=ContosoText
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj -mtriple=x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu-msil calls.ll -o lnx.o
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump --link-info lnx.o > lnx.sym
# RUN: FileCheck %s %{crash} --check-prefix=SYMTAB --input-file=lnx.sym
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SYMHDR --input-file=lnx.sym \
# RUN:   --implicit-check-not="{{(GLOBAL|WEAK) .*__msil_mc}}"
# RUN: msil-ld lnx.o --reference=refs -o lnx.exe 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump lnx.exe > lnx.txt
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=BIND,STUBS --input-file=lnx.txt
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ACCESS --input-file=lnx.txt
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=REFS --input-file=lnx.txt --implicit-check-not=assemblyref \
# RUN:   --implicit-check-not=mscorlib --implicit-check-not=msil.bcl --implicit-check-not=ContosoText
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj -mtriple=msil64-unknown-dotnet calls.ll -o net.o
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump --link-info net.o > net.sym
# RUN: FileCheck %s %{crash} --check-prefix=SYMTAB --input-file=net.sym
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SYMHDR --input-file=net.sym \
# RUN:   --implicit-check-not="{{(GLOBAL|WEAK) .*__msil_mc}}"
# RUN: msil-ld net.o --reference=refs -o net.exe 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump net.exe > net.txt
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=BIND,STUBS --input-file=net.txt
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ACCESS --input-file=net.txt
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=REFS --input-file=net.txt --implicit-check-not=assemblyref \
# RUN:   --implicit-check-not=mscorlib --implicit-check-not=msil.bcl --implicit-check-not=ContosoText

## The header line only: the implicit check-not then covers every symbol line.
# SYMHDR: {{^}}LinkInfo v1.0 {{.+$}}
# SYMTAB-DAG: {{^}}Symbol {{[0-9]+}} FUNCTION GLOBAL DEFAULT 'main' method=0x{{[0-9A-F]+}}{{$}}
# SYMTAB-DAG: {{^}}Symbol {{[0-9]+}} FUNCTION LOCAL DEFAULT '__msil_mc.prims' method=0x{{[0-9A-F]+}}{{$}}
# SYMTAB-DAG: {{^}}Symbol {{[0-9]+}} FUNCTION LOCAL DEFAULT '__msil_mc.mix' method=0x{{[0-9A-F]+}}{{$}}
# SYMTAB-DAG: {{^}}Symbol {{[0-9]+}} FUNCTION LOCAL DEFAULT '__msil_mc.ptrs' method=0x{{[0-9A-F]+}}{{$}}
# SYMTAB-DAG: {{^}}Symbol {{[0-9]+}} FUNCTION LOCAL DEFAULT '__msil_mc.describe' method=0x{{[0-9A-F]+}}{{$}}
# SYMTAB-DAG: {{^}}Symbol {{[0-9]+}} FUNCTION LOCAL DEFAULT '__msil_mc.widget_new' method=0x{{[0-9A-F]+}}{{$}}
# SYMTAB-DAG: {{^}}Symbol {{[0-9]+}} FUNCTION LOCAL DEFAULT '__msil_mc.length16' method=0x{{[0-9A-F]+}}{{$}}
# SYMTAB-DAG: {{^}}Symbol {{[0-9]+}} FUNCTION LOCAL DEFAULT '__msil_mc.length32' method=0x{{[0-9A-F]+}}{{$}}
# SYMTAB-DAG: {{^}}Symbol {{[0-9]+}} FUNCTION LOCAL DEFAULT '__msil_mc.check' method=0x{{[0-9A-F]+}}{{$}}
# SYMTAB-DAG: {{^}}Symbol {{[0-9]+}} FUNCTION LOCAL DEFAULT '__msil_mc.letter' method=0x{{[0-9A-F]+}}{{$}}
# SYMTAB-DAG: {{^}}Symbol {{[0-9]+}} FUNCTION LOCAL DEFAULT '__msil_mc.wrap' method=0x{{[0-9A-F]+}}{{$}}
# SYMTAB-DAG: {{^}}Symbol {{[0-9]+}} FUNCTION LOCAL DEFAULT '__msil_mc.origin' method=0x{{[0-9A-F]+}}{{$}}
# SYMTAB-DAG: {{^}}Symbol {{[0-9]+}} FUNCTION LOCAL DEFAULT '__msil_mc.set_mode' method=0x{{[0-9A-F]+}}{{$}}
# SYMTAB-DAG: {{^}}Symbol {{[0-9]+}} FUNCTION LOCAL DEFAULT '__msil_mc.set_wide' method=0x{{[0-9A-F]+}}{{$}}
# SYMTAB-DAG: {{^}}Symbol {{[0-9]+}} FUNCTION LOCAL DEFAULT '__msil_mc.set_small' method=0x{{[0-9A-F]+}}{{$}}
# SYMTAB-DAG: {{^}}Symbol {{[0-9]+}} FUNCTION LOCAL DEFAULT '__msil_mc.set_modes' method=0x{{[0-9A-F]+}}{{$}}
